<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Alamut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1256</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamut">Alamut</a> was the capture of the mountain fortress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> by Mongol forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> in 1256. It ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> state. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> profile places the event at the start of Hulagu's campaign that led to the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-alamut.jpg" alt="Siege of Alamut" width="275" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basawan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assassins2-alamut.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
